# ── Secrets and crypto material ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# ASP.NET Data Protection keys (crypto material — never commit)
TFE.Api/DataProtection-Keys/
# Azure publish profiles carry deployment credentials in clear text
*.PublishSettings
*.pubxml.user
appsettings.Local.json
# Claude Code per-machine overrides. Its command allow-list stores literal shell invocations, which
# is how an admin login (email + password) ended up committed here — see the audit of 2026-07-31.
# The shared, reviewable settings file (.claude/settings.json) stays tracked on purpose.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── .NET build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Regenerated by `dotnet restore` / `dotnet build`. Tracking them was actively harmful: the committed
# project.assets.json and *.nuget.g.props hold absolute paths from one developer's machine, which are
# meaningless on any other machine and on a CI runner.
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/

# Local publish output — the CI pipeline builds its own from source
publish/

# ── IDE / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Rédaction du TFE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sources du rapport écrit et ses diagrammes. Hors périmètre du dépôt applicatif : rien ici ne sert
# à construire ou déployer l'application, et ces fichiers suivent leur propre cycle de révision.
# Ancrés à la racine pour ne pas masquer un éventuel dossier docs/ d'un sous-projet.
/docs/
/rapport.md
